   "source": [
    "### Data overview\n",
    "\n",
    "For each dataset include the following information\n",
    "- Dataset #1\n",
    "  - Dataset Name: The Condemned\n",
    "  - Link to the dataset: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/theintercept/the-condemned-data/refs/heads/master/the-condemed-data.csv\n",
    "  - Number of observations: 7335\n",
    "  - Number of variables: 21\n",
    "  - Description of the variables most relevant to this project\n",
    "    Outcome Variables\n",
    "    - executed: Indicates whether the individual was executed.\n",
    "    - volunteer_execution: Indicates whether the individual waived appeals and voluntarily accepted execution.\n",
    "    - commuted: Indicates whether the death sentence was commuted by executive action.\n",
    "    - exonerated: Indicates whether the individual was exonerated of the charges.\n",
    "    - resentenced: Indicates whether the individual was resentenced to a non-death sentence.\n",
    "    - released: Indicates whether the individual was released from prison.\n",
    "    - died and suicide: Indicate whether the individual died or died by suicide while on death row.\n",
    "    - currently_on_death_row: Indicates whether the individual remains on death row at the time of the dataset’s most recent update.\n",
    "    Demographic Variables\n",
    "    - race: The recorded race of the individual, used to examine racial disparities in death row outcomes.\n",
    "    - gender: The recorded gender of the individual.\n",
    "    - DOB (Date of Birth): Used to calculate age at the time of sentencing.\n",
    "    Geographic Variables\n",
    "    - state: The U.S. state in which the individual was sentenced to death.\n",
    "    - county: The county of sentencing, reflecting local jurisdictional context.\n",
    "    Other\n",
    "    - sentencing_year: The year of sentencing, used to capture trends in capital punishment practices over time.\n",
    "    - current_sentence: Describes the individual’s current legal sentence following removal from death row or continued incarceration. Possible values include: DR: Death Row, LWOP: Life Without Parole, LPP: Life With Possibility of Parole, Y: Term of Years, M: Term of Months, TIME: Time Served\n",
    "\n",
    "  - Descriptions of any shortcomings this dataset has with repsect to the project\n",
    "    - The dataset does not include information about appeals, so we cannot directly account for its effects in our analysis.\n",
    "    - Information about the type of crime, victim characteristics, or severity of the offense is not available. These factors are important in legal decision-making and could help explain differences in outcomes. Without this information, we cannot determine whether observed patterns are due to case details or broader systemic factors.\n",
    "    - The dataset does not provide dates for executions, commutations, or exonerations. This makes it difficult to measure how long individuals spend on death row or to analyze how quickly different outcomes occur.\n",
    "    \n",
    "- Dataset #2 (if you have more than one!)\n",
    "  - same as above\n",
    "- etc\n",
    "\n",
    "Each dataset deserves either a set of bullet points as above or a few sentences if you prefer that method.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you plan to use multiple datasets, add a few sentences about how you plan to combine these datasets."
   ]
